FINAL REPORT — Human Activity Recognition with IMU Sensor Data
Project Title
Human Activity Recognition using the Daily and Sports Activities Dataset

Problem Statement

The goal is to classify 19 physical activities using sensor data from 5 body units. Each unit has 9 axes: accelerometer, gyroscope, and magnetometer. A segment is 5 seconds long with 125 time steps and 45 sensor channels. The model takes a segment as input and predicts which activity the person is doing.
This is useful for health apps, fitness tracking, and medical monitoring.\

Dataset

Name: Daily and Sports Activities Dataset
Source: UCI Machine Learning Repository
Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/256/daily+and+sports+activities
Total segments: 9120
Activities: 19
Subjects: 8 people
Segment length: 125 time steps at 25 Hz
Channels: 45 (5 body units x 9 axes)

Data Preprocessing

I split data by subject ID using GroupShuffleSplit. The same person cannot be in both train and test. Without this the model memorizes the person's movement style and gives fake high accuracy. This is called data leakage. Random split gave 97% accuracy. Subject-aware split gave the honest result.
Train: subjects 4, 5, 7, 8 — about 6384 segments
Validation: subjects 1, 3 — about 1368 segments
Test: subjects 2, 6 — about 1368 segments
I normalized each of the 45 channels with StandardScaler fitted only on training data.
Model Architectures
Random Forest baseline: I extracted 8 statistical features from each of 45 channels (mean, std, min, max, range, rms, zero-crossing rate, energy). Total: 360 features. Then trained a Random Forest with 100 trees.
1D CNN: 3 convolutional blocks with Conv1d, BatchNorm, ReLU, MaxPool. Then AdaptiveAvgPool and two fully connected layers. Input shape: (N, 45, 125).
BiLSTM: 2-layer bidirectional LSTM with hidden size 128, output 256. LayerNorm, Dropout, two fully connected layers. Gradient clipping with max norm 1.0.
Improved CNN: Same as CNN but with residual connections inside each block. Input added to output helps gradient flow. Data augmentation with Gaussian noise sigma 0.05 doubles the training set. Label smoothing 0.1 in the loss function.

Training Setup

Optimizer: Adam for all deep learning models
CNN: lr=0.001, StepLR, early stopping patience 10
BiLSTM: lr=0.001, ReduceLROnPlateau, early stopping patience 10
Improved CNN: lr=0.0005, CosineAnnealingLR, early stopping patience 12
The test set was never used during training or model selection. Only validation loss was used to select the best model.
Evaluation Metrics
Accuracy: percentage of correct predictions
F1-macro: average F1 score across all 19 classes, treats all classes equally

